252
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,160
You're being ridiculous.

253
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:15,460
Never mind.

254
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:18,740
Fortunately, we have an excuse for you to meet up with Miku again.

255
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:23,100
Apparently, she likes to have tea with the girls she's taken a shining to once a week.

256
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,080
That's what we'll aim for next.

257
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:29,380
And now, Miku Izayoi will sing her hit, Mermaid Love Story.

258
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:33,500
She has such a lovely voice.

259
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:34,900
I want to do that, too!

260
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:36,560
You want to go do karaoke?

261
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:38,880
No, I want to do what she's doing!

262
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:40,240
What? You mean the drums?

263
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:41,200
Ba-dum!

264
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:42,620
Ba-dum!

265
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:44,360
Ba-dum!

266
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:44,960
Ba-dum!

267
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,160
Ba-dum!

268
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:47,240
Ba-dum!

269
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,740
Ba-dum!

270
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:49,240
Ba-dum!

271
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:49,740
Ba-dum!

272
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:50,240
Ba-dum!

273
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:50,740
Ba-dum!

274
00:14:53,380 --> 00:14:54,200
They're here.

275
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,320
Is there something we can help you with?

276
00:14:59,620 --> 00:15:00,560
Uh, yes, please.

277
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,820
I met Miku in Tengu Square yesterday.

278
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,580
What, are you another fan?

279
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,360
Not exactly.

280
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:06,840
That's what they all say.

281
00:15:07,220 --> 00:15:09,400
I'm sorry, but this is supposed to be her private...

282
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,880
Hello again, Shiori.

283
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,280
Yo, what's up?

284
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,560
Ha-ha.

285
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:19,680
I wanted to say thanks.

286
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:21,700
You really shouldn't have gone to all this trouble.

287
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,120
No trouble at all.

288
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:25,900
I just had a very delicious tea blend delivered.

289
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:30,980
And it was so sweet of you to come all the way out here to my school just to return my handkerchief.

290
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:32,700
I had to share a cup with you.

291
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:35,100
This was supposed to be for those girls earlier, wasn't it?

292
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:37,000
Feels wrong to take their place.

293
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:38,780
Please, don't worry about them.

294
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:41,900
They're very obedient girls who always do what they've been told.

295
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:42,680
Ha-ha.

296
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:47,300
Wow, this is really good.

297
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:48,080
Ha-ha.

298
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,400
Everything's going smoothly.

299
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:02,020
We might be able to get her faster than we anticipated.

300
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:05,640
You know, you really are amazing.

301
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:08,060
I've never had anyone like you before.

302
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:08,640
Huh?

303
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:12,780
Shiori, don't you feel like there's something special between us?

304
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:15,560
I think that you should become a student at Rindouji.

305
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:16,360
What?

306
00:16:16,660 --> 00:16:19,980
Now, don't you worry your pretty head one little bit about your grades or the cost.

307
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:22,360
I will personally request that you be passed through.

308
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:23,440
Hang on a second.

309
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:26,300
It's kind of sudden to decide on something like that.

310
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,800
Please, please, sir.

311
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:34,600
I... the answer is still no.

312
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:38,260
Hey, Shiori?

313
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:39,680
What can I do for you?

314
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,200
Please take up all your clothes.

315
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:48,400
Hey, I think you're great, but I can't do that.

316
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:50,240
I'm confused.

317
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:52,160
Why aren't you doing what I tell you?

318
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,200
So what does that mean, then?

319
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:56,040
Are you a spirit as well?

320
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:59,720
There's no point in trying to hide it anymore.

321
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:04,360
After all, there's no way an ordinary person could disregard a direct order from me.

322
00:17:05,560 --> 00:17:07,900
And so I wonder, what in the world are you?

323
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:09,680
Are you a spirit?

324
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:15,460
Or worse, are you working for those wizards who have been trying to track me down and take me out?

325
00:17:17,060 --> 00:17:18,040
I am...

326
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:21,520
What should we do?

327
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:24,440
If we try to cover it up, it'll make things worse.

328
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:28,060
It's gonna be risky, but we should try negotiating with her.

329
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,360
Look, I'm not a spirit.

330
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:31,980
I'm not a wizard either.

331
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:32,840
Just human.

332
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:34,600
That is so unfortunate.

333
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:36,460
Lying doesn't become you.

334
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:39,720
But I do have an ability that seals spirit powers away.

335
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:42,060
What is that supposed to mean?

336
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,080
Just what it sounds like.

337
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:47,840
So far, I've successfully sealed the power of five spirits.

338
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:52,380
As long as your powers are completely sealed, the AST won't be able to find you.

339
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:55,460
Trust me, there's a way you can live peacefully in our world.

340
00:17:55,920 --> 00:17:58,360
I give you my word you won't have to be alone anymore.

341
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,900
Miku, trust me.

342
00:18:00,980 --> 00:18:02,020
I just want to help you.

343
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:06,300
You know something?

344
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,480
I believe you.

345
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:07,900
Seriously?

346
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:12,000
But I don't need you to seal my powers for me.

347
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:12,760
Hmm?

348
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:16,920
The way things are right now, I don't think I could be much happier.

349
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:19,420
I have my powers and a life of luxury.

350
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:21,440
What more could I possibly need?

351
00:18:21,940 --> 00:18:23,140
Just keep on pushing.

352
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:24,600
You have to convince her.

353
00:18:24,960 --> 00:18:29,040
Look, Miku, you caused a major spatial quake in front of the train station a few days ago.

354
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:29,940
But why?

355
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:33,200
I'm not sure you have total control of your powers like you think you do.

356
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:36,140
Oh, so you know about that nasty incident?

357
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:39,800
Your concern is touching, but honestly, you don't need to worry about me.

358
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:43,180
I've got absolute control over my powers.

359
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:46,580
The spatial quake I caused the other day was not by accident, sweetie.

360
00:18:46,580 --> 00:18:48,960
What could I do?

361
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:52,020
I'd never gotten a chance to sing at Tingo Arena before.

362
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:56,920
So naturally, when I passed it in front of the station, I suddenly felt the urge to sing.

363
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:58,920
Then I decided to let it go.

364
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:01,160
That's the reason you did it?

365
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:03,020
Yeah, I just couldn't help myself.

366
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:06,140
The desire to make music completely took me over.

367
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:08,580
If your friends had been there, they could have died.

368
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:10,420
Did that thought even occur to you, Miku?

369
00:19:10,960 --> 00:19:12,900
I suppose I would have been upset.

370
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:14,080
Really? You would?

371
00:19:14,340 --> 00:19:17,220
Then again, all the girls totally adore me no matter what.

372
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:21,260
I'm sure they would be satisfied knowing they had died for me.

373
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:25,600
Because they totally adore you?

374
00:19:25,940 --> 00:19:27,500
Shido, try to calm down.

375
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:31,340
Yes. I have legions of fans that love me with all their hearts.

376
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:34,800
They do whatever I ask, whenever I ask them to do it.

377
00:19:35,100 --> 00:19:37,960
Then you might want to know. I hate you.

378
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:40,300
Why's that?

379
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:43,080
You're intolerably arrogant and prideful.

380
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:48,300
Even if everyone in the world chose to accept a spoiled brat like you, I'd still hate your guts.

381
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:52,180
And as much as they'd love you, I'd hate you more.

382
00:19:57,320 --> 00:20:01,620
Hearing such harsh words from you, they make me want you even more.

383
00:20:02,620 --> 00:20:06,360
I have a burning desire to tease you mercilessly.

384
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:10,720
Until you come to me, crying, your face streaked with tears.

385
00:20:10,720 --> 00:20:14,360
And shout, I love you, Miku.

386
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,660
Dream on. I will never belong to you.

387
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:18,480
Oh?

388
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:22,940
Then why don't we play a little game?

389
00:20:23,340 --> 00:20:28,000
If your school somehow manages to win first place at the festival, then...

390
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,800
I'll agree to let you seal my powers right then and there.

391
00:20:31,240 --> 00:20:32,440
A tenu festival?

392
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:38,580
That's right. I'm already participating in the stage portion, so you should put together a performance too.

393
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:40,840
But... you've got a serious advantage.

394
00:20:41,360 --> 00:20:42,660
Well, that's your opinion.

395
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:46,980
The way I see it, I'm already doing you a big favor by allowing you to compete.

396
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:49,520
Now, the other side of the coin.

397
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:51,860
If Rindoji wins, I will have you.

398
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:55,580
Oh, and I also want each one of the spirits that you already sealed.

399
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:57,240
Will you agree to my terms?

400
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:58,960
Or do you want to run away?

401
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:03,760
Is this some kind of joke?

402
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:06,280
No. We're quite serious about it.

403
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:09,540
And if you have any issues with that, then you can simply go wait outside.

404
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:13,020
Did you say human targets? Oh, hell no. What is this crap?

405
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:16,060
We're after spirits here. We don't hunt down people.

406
00:21:16,420 --> 00:21:20,200
And not only that, the operation is in Tengu Square during the school festival.

407
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:23,340
You want to fight spirits in a place where you're guaranteed a crowd?

408
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:28,440
This is a part of the ceremony. A cordial greeting to our admired adversaries.

409
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:31,560
Wait, what are you saying? Hold on, Northe.

410
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:35,480
Make sure Origami Tobichi doesn't find out about any of this.

411
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:35,980
What?

412
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:38,380
That's also a direct order from the top.

413
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:41,260
If you have any concerns, feel free to tell them.

414
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:44,860
What on earth was that about?

415
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:50,820
Shido Itsuka? Where have I heard that name?

416
00:21:50,820 --> 00:21:54,900
No. Wasn't he Origami's...?

417
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:02,460
That's a complete voyage

418
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:17,080
The story of the futurist

419
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:19,100
I am the plans that I have built on patents

420
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:49,080
Thank you.

421
00:22:49,100 --> 00:23:19,080
Thank you.

422
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:21,100
Thank you.

